"P1593895644" "Destroy the Tracking Computer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2735811562" "You destroyed the tracking computer, but found some disturbing information."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2082713349" "You've destroyed the tracking computer, only to discover that the Syndicate was one step ahead of you!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2136027771" "<color BurlyWood>Good timing, {HeroName}. Just talked with Paolo, said his brother is with his father now, we've got one of our trams ready to get them out of the city. Have a little <i>complication</i> with Paolo though.<br><br>Huh? Problem on your end? No, no no no no, no problems on your end! Why are you having problems on your end?! We're not supposed to have problems, knew this smelled bad from the beginning, had a feeling, gut feeling! I can't handle this, I'm not supposed to handle this, not meant to handle this! Just supposed to bring people from A to B, not fight a giant crusade!<br><br>Syndicate know where ALL of the people we've helped to rescue are?! No, no no no no no! What do we do?! Too many complications! We're all gonna get chomped!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1360270754" "{HeroName}, glad you can make it. I'm Paolo Marino, I've heard a lot about you. Sorry that this is the first time we were able to meet.<br><br>I came here to take down the VP, but something came up.<br><br>I'm wanted down at the station...can I count on you to handle things here?<br><br>Just...one bit of a warning though. The PPD, they know I'm here. They think I'm here to take down a Syndicate cell, so if I leave...well...I'll have to call in PPD reinforcements to come attack the area."
// Answer Text :
"P3262390263" "Why aren't you leaving with your father and brother?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2822432178" "It has to be this way, {HeroName}. I <i>hate</i> the PPD and what they've become. But I need to stay in this position to make sure that my father and brother are safe.<br><br>Even if it means being in an organization that I hate...it's worth it, knowing my family is happy. We've already gone through enough hardships after my sister died this year.<br><br> I'm sorry that I made you go through all this, only to just walk away from your hard work. I really am.<br><br>And I want you to know that I am <i>very</i> sorry that I'll have to call the PPD down here - I need to do this to make everything look believable."
// Answer Text :
"P3330293747" "(Think on matters for a moment)"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P2583736022" "<color orange>If Paolo were to keep his current position, he would still be leading groups of PPD against the Resistance. Sure, he may be leading them away from his family and other people in the Resistance, but he'll still be leading PPD troops <i>against</i> the Resistance. This is fairly clear now - if you let him go, he'll be forced to call a squad of PPD down on you.<br><br>Of course, you could always <i>force</i> Paolo to be with his father and brother, which would involve knocking him out. Paolo may want to make a sacrifice for his family, but is that worth putting other members of the Resistance, yourself included, in danger?"
// Answer Text :
"P874810824" "(Let Paolo go and continue his work with the PPD)"
// Answer Text :
"P1155824906" "(Force Paolo to leave Praetoria to be with his family)"
// Answer Text :
"P899543006" "(Execute Paolo for being a traitor to Praetoria)"
// Page LeavePaolo Text :
"P650029664" "I'll be off then, {HeroName}. I wish you the best of luck."
// Answer Text :
"P2741651530" "You too, Paolo."
// Page ForcePaolo Text :
"P4153725982" "<color orange>You lunge forward to attack Paolo!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1235086192" "(Attack!)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3058500557" "We're living in dangerous times, {HeroName}. No doubt you have some news to report regarding the Resistance?"
// Answer Text :
"P3299455636" "No, I have news regarding the PPD - a man named Paolo Marino."
// Answer Text :
"P1872005079" "I do, but first, did the tracking beacon I placed lead to anything?"
// Page Tracking Text :
"P2013665454" "It did...somewhat.<br><br>Bella had it on her for quite some time - I don't believe she knew we were tracking her.<br><br>That, or, as we discovered, she handed it off to someone else shortly afterwards.<br><br>The tracker died deep beneath the tunnels, unfortunately. This did lead to an interesting development - that of a possible secret entrance into the Resistance base."
// Answer Text :
"P2435364844" "And what about this Dark Watcher that she mentioned?"
// Page DarkWatcher Text :
"P2474073582" "We're still looking into who exactly he is.<br><br>We don't have any records of a 'Dark Watcher' ever passing through the Powers Division, so he may be someone the Resistance snuck away from us. Or perhaps a super-powered being from outside of Praetoria."
// Answer Text :
"P3372457943" "I see. Well, I have news regarding the PPD - a man named Paolo Marino."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P618805645" "Paolo? The sergeant tasked with heading up with our new investigations? What about him?"
// Answer Text :
"P663498616" "He's a traitor. He's been working with the Resistance all along."
// Page Traitor Text :
"P986571639" "Hrm...this is disturbing, an officer of such high-ranking a traitor?<br><br>This doesn't bode well, {HeroName}.<br><br>I'm afraid you'll have no choice, I need you to <color red>deliver the fate that all traitors receive.</color> I am officially giving you the responsibility of carrying out his sentence. You will not face any problems for what you are about to do, I promise you that."
// Answer Text :
"P186832969" "And the list with the location of those the Resistance helped?"
// Page Helped Text :
"P1751441145" "You'll have to hand it over to the Resistance.<br><br>I would love for us to keep it, but doing so would reveal your true nature to the Resistance. It's far too early to reveal our trump card just yet. I hope you understand."
// Answer Text :
"P3862896563" "I do, Marchand. I'll speak with you again soon."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1000055441" "<color BurlyWood>Ugggh, I don't like this! Paolo found out about issue, he's running over to deal with this VP now, but he can't deal with the VP, stupid stupid stupid!<br><br>Problem came up with Paolo, PPD launching campaign to search for all the people that we've gotten out of the city. Fate really hates us, <i>really</i> hates us, since the powers that be in PPD chose <i>Paolo</i> as the lead investigator on the assignment. Really annoying!<br><br>What does he do? I want him to run, and he decides to stay, we do all this hard work and now he's staying! Says he's going to make sure no one is found, giving up being with his family. What about the work that I did?! Just throwing it away?!<br><br>Anyway, {HeroName}, we need to do something. Paolo found out the location of that VP who has the info, Daniel Shapiro, says he's going to tie this loose end up, but Paolo is an idiot.<br><br>You've gotta get to the lab where Shap is and get the information from him! "
// AcceptString :
"P3716872864" "What about Paolo? He'll be there, right?"
// SendOffString :
"P4241475663" "<color BurlyWood>Just stop him from doing anything stupid, knew he would do something stupid like this, sensed it from the start. Don't really care if he's gonna choose to stay in Praetoria now, causing me too much trouble, just wanted this to be simple, really simple! What's important is getting that info from the VP, can't have us being used by the Syndicate, too much to handle, too much responsibility on my shoulders to keep all of us free from them.<br><br><color yellow>Those Loyalists who are <i>truly</i> loyal to safety and peace of Praetoria would do well to speak with Provost Marchand about events that are happening.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2551316130" "Retrieve Survivor List from the Syndicate"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2356749612" "<color BurlyWood>Don't tell me you're here to say you can't do this, I don't need that, it's the last thing I need, the very last thing, right next to being chomped."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3532186859" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Praetoria's Best Officer</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2021388939" "Daniel Shapiro, VP of Public Relations in Syfotine Industries, is here somewhere with the list. You'll have to carve a path through the Syndicate to get to him and free the Resistance."

